# MCP Server — Tu Descuento Colombia

HTTP streamable MCP server that exposes tools, prompts, and resources so an AI support agent can talk to the Tu Descuento CRM.

## Key paths

- `src/server.ts` — Express + `StreamableHTTPServerTransport` (`POST/GET/DELETE /mcp`) with Bearer auth
- `src/middleware/` — `auth.ts` (multi-token Bearer) and `rate-limit.ts`
- `src/config/auth-tokens.ts` — registry loaded from `MCP_AUTH_TOKENS`
- `src/tools/` — MCP tools via `McpServer.registerTool` (Zod + annotations)
- `src/services/` — API clients extending `BaseService`
- `src/types/entities/` — CRM entity types; re-exported from `src/types/index.ts`
- `src/prompts/`, `src/resources/` — MCP prompts and static resources
- `docs/` — Project documentation index in `docs/README.md` (auth: `docs/security/AUTHENTICATION.md`)

## Build & run

```bash
npm run build   # tsc + tsc-alias (required for @/ path resolution)
npm start
npm run dev
npm run gen:token -- --name my-client
```

Test via Postman JSON-RPC against `POST http://localhost:3000/mcp` with `Authorization: Bearer …`. See `docs/integrations/POSTMAN_TESTS.md` and `docs/security/AUTHENTICATION.md`.

## Import aliases (mandatory)

From `tsconfig.json`: `@/*`, `@services/*`, `@tools/*`. Always append `.js` in imports (ESM):

```typescript
import { BaseService } from '@services/base-service.js'
```

## New tool checklist (4–5 files)

1. `src/types/entities/[entity].ts`
2. Export in `src/types/index.ts`
3. `src/services/[entity]-service.ts`
4. `src/tools/[entity]/[tool].ts` — export `registerX(server)` (one tool per file)
5. Add registrar to `src/tools/index.ts` → `registerAllTools`

Prefer the `mcp-tool-creator` skill and `crm-api-researcher` / `mcp-tool-builder` subagents when implementing CRM-backed tools.
